fastlowess provides the upstream CMake target:

    find_package(fastlowess CONFIG REQUIRED)
    target_link_libraries(main PRIVATE fastlowess::fastlowess)

Include <fastlowess.hpp> to use the C++17 interface. The port supports Windows
x64/ARM64 with MSVC, glibc Linux x64/ARM64, and macOS x64/ARM64. Shared linkage
is required. The Linux target compiler is checked for glibc during configuration;
musl targets are not supported by this curated port and require an overlay.
Windows uses the release CRT. Debug and Release consumers both use the upstream
Release library. Rust and Cargo are not required.